+
+### Tuning HY4 heterogeneous MoE
+
+```bash
+python op_tests/tuners/tune_fhmoe.py \
+  -i aiter/configs/tuned_fhmoe.csv \
+  -o aiter/configs/tuned_fhmoe.csv \
+  --tokens 1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128,256,512,1024,2048,4096,8192,16384,32768 \
+  --profile /tmp/hy4_fhmoe_profile.csv
+```
+
+Add `--quick` for the bounded pair-beam search used by tuning pipeline smoke
+tests. Quick mode intentionally excludes nonzero XCD-swizzle candidates and
+does not prove the production optimum. Without it, the tuner evaluates the full
+valid stage-1 x stage-2 product; the default all-bucket sweep can take hours, so
+exhaustive tuning should normally target selected `--tokens`. The tuner
+optimizes the isolated FHMoE call; only commit changed rows after a matched
+serving-level A/B test because full-model scheduling can favor a different
+kernel.
+
+For a floor bucket that serves larger runtime shapes, keep the CSV key in
+`--tokens` and provide the representative runtime M separately. For example:
+
+```bash
+python op_tests/tuners/tune_fhmoe.py \
+  -i aiter/configs/tuned_fhmoe.csv \
+  -o aiter/configs/tuned_fhmoe.csv \
+  --tokens 32768 \
+  --benchmark-token 38836
+```
+
+`--benchmark-token` requires exactly one `--tokens` bucket, must be positive
+and no greater than 38836, and must resolve to the selected bucket. HY4 uses
+the global power-of-two tiers below 32768 and the 32768 row through its safety
+limit. Larger values are rejected until reduce output supports addressing
+beyond 4 GiB.
+
+Candidate error checks are baseline-relative regression guards, not independent
+oracles. Before updating each CSV row, the final selected full-M output is also
+checked against an independent FP32 reference for representative token rows
+covering every routed expert for M>=32 (and every expert reachable by smaller
+buckets) plus the shared expert. Use
+`--sampled-reference-tolerance` to adjust that final acceptance threshold.
+`--tolerance` controls baseline-relative candidate accuracy, while
+`--stability-tolerance` independently bounds repeat-output relative L2
+(default `8e-3`); it is not a timing-jitter threshold.
+
+Profile CSV columns are
+`token,runtime_token,stage,kernel,ms,error`. Rows are committed incrementally
+and replaced by `(token, runtime_token)`, so interrupted or resumed runs retain
+completed measurements. Each token's profile rows are committed before its
+tuned output row, so a profile-write failure leaves that token uncommitted and
+safe to retry. Legacy five-column profiles are migrated with `runtime_token=token`.
+
+When input and output are different files, resume from the partial output, not
+the original input, and select only unfinished buckets:
+
+```bash
+python op_tests/tuners/tune_fhmoe.py \
+  -i /tmp/partial_tuned_fhmoe.csv \
+  -o /tmp/partial_tuned_fhmoe.csv \
+  --tokens <remaining-comma-separated-buckets> \
+  --profile /tmp/hy4_fhmoe_profile.csv
 ```
 
